# results-orig: the original dr.exe's version of results.keys, for
#   make docker-test ORIG=1 SCENARIO=results-orig SECS=280
#
# Two differences from results.keys, both measured.
#
# 1. The intro-skip prefix. The original shows two extra publisher splash
#    screens before its own intro/menu (Apogee, then Remedy) that our port
#    does not render; measured with staggered shot:s1..s4 checkpoints:
#      t=13s (1 Enter):  still on the Apogee splash
#      t=17s (2 Enters): Remedy splash
#      t=21s (3 Enters): main menu, "Start Racing" highlighted
#      t=25s (4 Enters): already one level into "Start Racing" (overshoot)
#    So the original needs three Enters where the port needs one; from the
#    main menu through the sign-up screen it reuses results.keys's waits
#    unchanged, since an earlier trial found the original and the port
#    track each other exactly once both are past their respective intros
#    (under CrossOver an identical key sequence
#    reached the identical Driver's Licence screen in both).
# 2. The race-finish wait. A first attempt at 155s (results.keys's value,
#    which was enough for our port) caught the original's race still
#    running at t=216s (out/results.png showed lap 1/4, not the results
#    screen). Whether that is the original always racing longer or one
#    slow track by chance is not established; 200s plus margin is used
#    here rather than re-measuring further.
enter w3000
enter w3000
enter w3500
shot:menu
enter w1500
enter w1500
t w200
e w200
s w200
t w200
enter w1200
shot:licence
enter w1500
enter w3000
enter w2500
enter w20000
enter w2000
shot:race
w200000
enter w4000
shot:results
